{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaMTCLocalizationObligation","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt"],"declarations":31,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke.bwLocalization_loc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke.bwLocalization_loc","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L253-L257","doc":"The BW localization measure equals the Hecke Plancherel measure `d_q²/D²` (the discharged\nresidual-(i) obligation, conditional on the identification). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke.bwLocalization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke.bwLocalization","kind":"def","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L247-L251","doc":"**Residual (i) holds given the identification.** The BW localization (squared gauge vacuum row)\nis a `BeasleyWittenLocalization` whose measure is the Hecke Plancherel measure `d_q²/D²` — so C1\n(`Σ=1`), C2 (chirality), C6 (full support) all follow from the single conjecture `bwS0_eq_hecke`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke.toVerlindeModularData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke.toVerlindeModularData","kind":"def","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L232-L245","doc":"The modular tensor category built from the (conjectured) BW vacuum-row identification: the gauge\nrow `bwS0` is the S-matrix vacuum row, the q-dimensions are the Hecke `d_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke.bwS0_eq_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke.bwS0_eq_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L226-L226","doc":"**THE single open conjecture (owner-gated):** the gauge-defined vacuum S-matrix row equals the\nHecke modular datum `d_q(λ)/√(Σ d_q²)`. What the published localization must deliver; foreclosed on\nthe SU(2)`_k` sub-route, so full-Hecke.\n\n**Realized at the fibre root** (PR #4365): the LR/WRT amplitude satisfies `|A_m(α)| = 2·[mark]/D`\nexactly at the root of unity `ζ = e^{iπ/5}` (`KeystoneLRAmplitudeReal.amplitude_first` /\n`colored_modulus_phi_node`), i.e. `bwS0 = d_ζ/D` for the *actual* gauge datum (the WRT amplitude),\nnot the fiat. So the residual open content is precisely the **archimedean continuation of `bwS0`\nfrom `ζ` to real `q₀`** — and the value-map side of that continuation is polynomial evaluation\n(`KeystoneWLambdaContinuation`), so the wall is the continuation of the *gauge row*, not the\nPlancherel structure (proved here) nor the value map (proved). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke.bwS0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke.bwS0","kind":"def","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L214-L214","doc":"**The gauge datum** — the BW localization's vacuum S-matrix row on the blocks, abstract (the\npath-integral output on `S³/2I`, NOT defined as `d_q/D`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke.hP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke.hP","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L211-L211","doc":"The block set is nonempty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke.hconj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke.hconj","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L209-L209","doc":"The blocks are closed under transpose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke.hsorted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke.hsorted","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L207-L207","doc":"The blocks are weakly-decreasing partitions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke.hq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke.hq","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L205-L205","doc":"Substrate regime `q > 1` (positivity of the Hecke q-dimensions). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke.mk","kind":"ctor","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L203-L203","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.BWVacuumRowIsHecke","kind":"class","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L185-L226","doc":"**The single open content of residual (i), precisely stated — the category identification.**\n\nIntroduce the Beasley–Witten localization's vacuum S-matrix row `bwS0` as an **abstract gauge\ndatum**: the Chern–Simons path-integral output on `S³/2I`, carried as an opaque field — **not**\ndefined as `d_q/D`. The lone open conjecture is `bwS0_eq_hecke`: that the gauge-defined vacuum row\nequals the Hecke modular datum `d_q(λ)/√(Σ d_q²)`. This is the *one* thing the published, owner-gated\nlocalization must deliver; everything else in residual (i) — the Verlinde measure `= d_q²/D²`, C1\n(`Σ=1`), C2 (chirality), C6 (full support) — is **derived** from it (`bwLocalization`,\n`bwLocalization_loc`).\n\nNo global instance is supplied: residual (i) is genuinely conditional on this identification, which is\nowner-gated (the narrow Subgoal-2 reversal, #2503/#2524) and **foreclosed on the SU(2)`_k` sub-route**\n(`Su2SchurWeylForeclosure.lean`, #2717/#2727 — `[2j+1]_q ≠ d_q(λ)` off the standard rep, so the index\nmust live full-Hecke side). The class field `bwS0_eq_hecke` is a content-bearing,\nparameter-quantified identity (AGENTS.md §3b-tax — primary conjecture, not `True`); the inhabiting\n`example` below is the *fiat* realization (`bwS0 := d_q/D`), present only to show the conditional\nresults are not conditional-on-`False`. The genuinely open content is the *physical* instance, where\n`bwS0` is the actual path-integral output. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.heckeVerlindeData_loc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.heckeVerlindeData_loc","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L170-L181","doc":"**The Hecke Verlinde data reproduces the residual-(i) localization with the S-matrix explicit.**\n`(heckeVerlindeData …).toBeasleyWitten` has `loc = (d_q/D)²` and matches `d_q²/D²` — the same measure\nas `heckeLocalizationOfPos`, now exhibited as the squared vacuum S-matrix row of the (conjectured)\nlocalization category. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.heckeVerlindeData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.heckeVerlindeData","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L145-L168","doc":"**The Hecke q-dimensions realize `VerlindeModularData`** for `q > 1` on any conjugate-closed,\nnonempty block set `P`: take `qDim := d_q`, `D := √(Σ d_q²)`, `S0 := d_q/D`. Then `S0_eq` is `rfl`\nand the modular-data fields are discharged from positivity (`qDim_pos`, `sum_qDimSq_pos`) and the\ncorpus `qDim_conj`. The **only** thing this does *not* establish is the physics — that the BW\nlocalization of `S³/2I` actually *is* this category; that owner-gated identification is the open\nresidual. Given it, `toBeasleyWitten ∘ heckeVerlindeData` reproduces `heckeLocalizationOfPos` with\nthe S-matrix made explicit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.verlindeData_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.verlindeData_two","kind":"instance","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L123-L139","doc":"**Non-vacuity model — the `n = 2` modular category over `ℝ`.** Two blocks `[2],[1,1]`, both of\nquantum dimension `1`, `D = √2` (`D² = 2 = Σ d²`), vacuum row `S_{00} = 1/√2`. Confirms\n`VerlindeModularData` is inhabited, so the bridge and `toBeasleyWitten` are not vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.toBeasleyWitten","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.toBeasleyWitten","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L103-L117","doc":"**The bridge discharges the residual-(i) obligation.** Any `VerlindeModularData` (a modular\ncategory produced by the localization, with vacuum row `S_{0λ}=d_λ/D`) yields a\n`BeasleyWittenLocalization` whose `loc` is the squared vacuum S-matrix row — and `loc_matches` is the\nbridge `verlindeMeasure_eq_plancherel`. So once the localization is identified as *this* modular\ncategory, residual (i)'s C1/C2/C6 consequences all follow. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.sum_qDimSq_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.sum_qDimSq_ne","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L99-L101","doc":"`Σ qDim² ≠ 0` — from `D² = Σ qDim²` and `D ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.verlindeMeasure_eq_plancherel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.verlindeMeasure_eq_plancherel","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L92-L97","doc":"**The DG bridge (sorry-free): the localization measure IS the Hecke Plancherel measure.**\n`μ(λ) = S_{0λ}² = (d_λ/D)² = d_λ²/D²`. The gauge-theory output (squared vacuum S-matrix row) equals\n`d_q²/D²` purely from the published modular-data identity `S_{0λ} = d_λ/D` — no fit, no extra input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.verlindeMeasure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.verlindeMeasure","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L88-L90","doc":"**The Verlinde measure** `μ(λ) = S_{0λ}²` — the squared vacuum S-matrix row, i.e. the genuine\nBeasley–Witten localization weight on the blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.S0_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.S0_eq","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L82-L82","doc":"**Published modular-data identity** `S_{0λ} = d_λ/D` (vacuum row of the S-matrix in any\nmodular tensor category). The gauge output, now a structural fact rather than a raw measure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.S0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.S0","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L79-L79","doc":"The **vacuum S-matrix row** `S_{0λ}` — the Beasley–Witten / Verlinde localization output. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.D_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.D_ne","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L77-L77","doc":"`D ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.D_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.D_sq","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L75-L75","doc":"`D² = Σ_λ d_q(λ)²` — the defining global-dimension relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.D","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.D","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L73-L73","doc":"The global quantum dimension `D` (total dimension of the modular category). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.qDim_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.qDim_conj","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L71-L71","doc":"`d_q(λ′) = d_q(λ)` (corpus-proved, `KeystoneC2QDimTranspose.qDim_conj`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.qDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.qDim","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L69-L69","doc":"The categorical quantum dimension `d_q(λ)` (the *Hecke* q-dimension on an instance). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.conj_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.conj_mem","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L67-L67","doc":"Blocks closed under transpose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.conj","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L65-L65","doc":"The transpose involution `λ ↦ λ′`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.parts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.parts","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L63-L63","doc":"The finite set of Hecke partition blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.Part","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.Part","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L61-L61","doc":"Partition index for the Hecke block `λ ⊢ n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.VerlindeModularData","kind":"class","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.lean#L48-L82","doc":"**Modular data of the Beasley–Witten / RT localization category** (the gauge-theory side,\nsharpened). The localization on `S³/2I` outputs a modular tensor category whose vacuum S-matrix row\n`S0` weights the Verlinde measure. This class carries that modular data: the Hecke blocks, the\ncategorical quantum dimension `qDim`, the global dimension `D` (`D² = Σ qDim²`), and the vacuum\nS-matrix row `S0`. In *any* modular category the vacuum row is `S_{0λ} = d_λ/D` (`S0_eq`) — a\n**published structural fact** (Bakalov–Kirillov / EGNO), carried here as the modular-data input, *not*\na fit. The single physics content — that this category's `qDim` is the *Hecke* `d_q` — lives in\n*constructing an instance*, not in these fields.\n\n-- Ref: [bakalovkirillov2001] Lectures on Tensor Categories and Modular Functors (S-matrix vacuum row).\n-- Ref: [beasleywitten2005] https://doi.org/10.4310/jdg/1143593746 — non-abelian CS localization. ","signatureChunk":0}]}